        "Abstract": "Language models for historical states of language are becoming increasingly important to allow the optimal digitisation and analysis of old textual sources. In this paper, we present our efforts to develop NLP tools for Early Modern French. We present the FREEMmax corpus of Early Modern French and D'AlemBERT, a RoBERTa-based language model trained on FREEMmax. We evaluate the usefulness of D'AlemBERT by fine-tuning it on a part-of-speech tagging task, outperforming previous work on the test set."
